{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>In your mouth and in your heart to do it.</b> He mentioned here three things: the mouth, the heart, and the deed. <b>And behold,</b> all the commandments are included in these three parts, for there are commandments that depend on the mouth, some that depend on the heart, and some on deed. And upon this the Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: 'On three things the world stands — on Torah, on worship, and on deeds of lovingkindness.' 'On Torah' — this is 'in your mouth'; 'on worship' — this is 'in your heart,' which is the worship of the heart; 'on deeds of lovingkindness' — this is 'to do it.' And it is well known that the commandments that depend on the heart are a greater worship to the Holy One, blessed be He, than the commandments that depend on speech; therefore the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: one who interrupts words of Torah in order to recite Shema — and they said of the first verse, this is the Shema of Rabbi Yehudah ha-Nasi. And those that depend on speech are a greater worship than those that depend on deed; therefore they said: Torah is greater than all the sacrifices, as it is said (Leviticus 7): ״זאת התורה לעולה למנחה ולחטאת ולאשם ולמלואים ולזבח השלמים״. And because of this he mentioned 'and in your heart' in the middle, for its importance above them all, and mentioned 'to do it' after it. And the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote: 'in your mouth and in your heart' is the matter of confession upon repentance that he mentioned above, and he said that 'this commandment' was said concerning repentance, in which one is commanded, as he said, ״ושבת עד ה' אלהיך״, and he said, ״לא נפלאת היא״ and ״לא רחוקה״ — for even when they are in the land of their enemies in exile and they are driven away and scattered, they are able to return in repentance in every place they are, even if they were at the end of the world — ״קרוב אליך הדבר מאד״ to do it in these two things: in your mouth and in your heart, that you agree in your thought and resolve in your heart and confess with your mouth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:52:30.536832220Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}